positions.description:
Build innovative and performant features into our Customer Success platform using the latest engineering practices and technologies.
Upgrade frontend codebase from deprecated JavaScript/TypeScript framework to use a more current version;
Collaborate with cross-functional teams to ensure a smooth transition, minimizing downtime and user impact during framework upgrades;

Built Content Management System internal tools and applications to improve the company’s content creation process;
Worked with product managers to groom, estimate, prioritize, and assign dev tasks;
Converted design wireframes into fully composed prototypes and functional components/applications;
Shipped high-quality, maintainable, extensible code on time in adherence to SDLC, best practices, and design/style guides;
Provided constructive, actionable feedback to members of the engineering team;
Mentored junior developers through peer programming exercises and constructive code reviews;
Coordinated and managed code deployments;
Interviewed, evaluated, and recruited engineering candidates;

Completely rebuilt the marketing website; Improved several SEO page speed metrics such as FCP, LCP, & TTI;
Increased marketing website’s mobile page experience from 20% to 90%;
Rebuilt content catalog search application;
Helped rebuild our interactive content learning experience;
Built customer checkout UI experience;
Cleaned up code base and enforced best-practice standards;
Supported and maintained production systems when alerts are escalated to the engineering team;

Taught 20 students how to build web applications using a wide variety of the latest technologies and methods;
Developed curriculum to keep lessons update to date with current and emerging web technologies such as ES7, React JS, Node, and Express;
Graded and provided feedback on labs, assessments, homework, and projects

Assisted in teaching a pilot course on computer science fundamentals:
data structures and algorithms;
Facilitated daily Scrums and one-on-one meetings with students;
Gathered and analyzed surveys and feedback everyday from students to help improve the curriculum for future implementation;

Managed a team of five staff members in the Third Party Clients Department, maintained the database, analyzed reports, tracked stats, and processed client invoices averaging $20,000 on a daily basis;
Provided administrative support for a visa consulting agency contracted by the Embassy of India and servicing Indian nationals;
Networked between departments as a Sales Force operator to fulfill upwards to 10 office project deadlines per day and satisfy customer needs aligning with company expectations.

Promoted to Senior Branch Coordinator to manage branch location and took on supervisory responsibilities of six teachers;
Succeeded in increasing classroom performance standards of over 130 students and six teachers by leading weekly staff meetings which covered new and old training and reported areas of improvement and creating solutions;
I taught over 130 students English Language in basic, elementary, intermediate, advanced, and business using the Communicative method.

